  (text "LED logic level shifting and voltage stabilization"
    (at 146.05 157.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 8511c062-622a-437b-b790-e85c8f1a0d6c)
  )
  (text "Configuration Details\n\n1. Wireless nice!nano with nice!view (ZMK only)\n  - SPI pins are shared between nice!view and sensor\n  a. with SPI trackball\n    - connect MOTION(VIK-GPIO2) to MCU-MISO (same as I2C)\n  b. with SPI touchpad\n    - uses extra 3-pin header for DR (GPIO2)\n  c. with I2C touchpad\n    - SPI/I2C jumpers to SPI for nice!view\n    - uses extra 3-pin header for I2C and DR (GPIO2)\n    - I2C on low-speed pins, not ideal\n    - populate pull-up resistors R2, R3\n2. Wired RP2040 with LEDs\n  a. with SPI trackball (ZMK only, QMK does not support the PMW3610)\n  b. with I2C touchpad (ZMK or QMK)\n    - populate pull-up resistors R2, R3\n  c. with SPI touchpad (QMK only)\n    - QMK doesn't use DR pin, no need to connect GPIO2\n3. Wired RP2040 with nice!view\n  - can't have LEDs at the same time because LED pin acts as CS for nice!view\n  a. with SPI trackball (ZMK only)\n    - connect MOTION(VIK-GPIO2) to MCU-MISO (same as I2C)\n  b. with SPI touchpad (QMK only)\n    - QMK doesn't use DR pin, no need to connect GPIO2\n4. Wireless nice!nano with or w/o LEDs (ZMK only)\n  - uses 3.3V power for LEDs, out-of-spec\n  - high idle power draw if LEDs are populated\n    - 3.3V power cannot be turned off at the controller (needed by sensor)\n  a. with SPI trackball\n    - connect MOTION(VIK-GPIO2) to MCU-MISO (same as I2C)\n  b. with I2C touchpad\n    - populate pull-up resistors R2, R3\n  c. with SPI touchpad\n    - requires extra 3-pin header for DR pin\n\nBypass jumpers can be used to bypass Top, and/or Bottom LEDs and the level shifter.\nThis allows populating only some LEDs on the bottom PCB without top LEDs, or connecting\nthe VIK LED directly (not used in current keyboard). Level shifting is only needed with\n5V RAW power supply on wired controllers and can be bypassed otherwise.\n\nThe VIK_LED and VIK_5V jumpers should not be closed when connecting a Cirque touchpad.\nThey are also not needed with a trackball, so there is currently no reason to ever\nclose them. VIK_5V does not provide the correct voltage with wireless controllers."
    (at 172.72 360.68 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid 8dc631f6-67c5-46c7-b1ae-8d857309ceb2)
  )
  (text "Switch Matrix" (at 100.33 30.48 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid bcff69ef-9fa6-4b3a-b6d5-b8cf8799152d)
  )
  (text "I2C" (at 43.18 179.07 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid ed857f1a-dde0-411e-8a76-c64f88020147)
  )
  (text "Vik output and FFC connection to Top PCB" (at 194.31 218.44 0)
